Wire together all four pieces: framing wraps each send/recv, AEAD encrypts the
payload, the envelope header becomes the AAD, and the key comes from the module
parameter. The handshake is a simple encrypted HELLO exchange to confirm both
sides share the same key before entering the command loop. On any error (auth
failure, disconnect), release the AEAD transform, close the socket, sleep, and
retry the entire connection.
